{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedShapeRun","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedShapeRun","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedMaxCorner"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.removeCornerSteps_insertWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.removeCornerSteps_insertWord","kind":"theorem","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedShapeRun.lean#L171-L178","doc":"And such a run peels the shape to nothing — the second hypothesis of\n`insertWord_uninsertSteps_of_shape`, also inhabited. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.shapeCornersAlong_insertWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.shapeCornersAlong_insertWord","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedShapeRun.lean#L163-L169","doc":"**The shape-level condition is inhabited**, by every insertion-built run — brick 15 read through\nthe iff. Worth stating for the same reason brick 15 was: a reduction to a condition nothing\nsatisfies would be no reduction at all. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.cornersAlong_iff_shape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.cornersAlong_iff_shape","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedShapeRun.lean#L157-L161","doc":"**The two run conditions are the same condition.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.shapeCornersAlong_of_cornersAlong","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.shapeCornersAlong_of_cornersAlong","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedShapeRun.lean#L143-L155","doc":"**The tableau-level corner condition implies the shape-level one.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertWord_uninsertSteps_of_shape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertWord_uninsertSteps_of_shape","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedShapeRun.lean#L113-L132","doc":"**The `P`-side conclusion, from shapes alone.** If the run's positions are corners of the shape\nand peel it down to nothing, the word it recovers has `T` as its insertion tableau.\n\nEvery hypothesis is now about `T`'s **shape** and the position list — `P` itself appears only in the\nconclusion. That is the whole point of the reduction: what remains for surjectivity is to produce\n`ShapeCornersAlong` and the emptying condition from a standard recording tableau, with the\ninsertion tableau no longer involved. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.tableauShape_uninsertSteps","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.tableauShape_uninsertSteps","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedShapeRun.lean#L106-L111","doc":"The shape the run returns, on its own. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.cornersAlong_of_shape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.cornersAlong_of_shape","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedShapeRun.lean#L100-L104","doc":"The tableau-level corner condition, on its own. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.uninsertSteps_shape_and_corners","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.uninsertSteps_shape_and_corners","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedShapeRun.lean#L74-L98","doc":"**The reduction.** A shape-level corner condition delivers the tableau-level one, together with\nthe shape of the tableau the run returns.\n\nBoth conclusions are proved in one induction because neither is available without the other — see\nthe module docstring. The step is: the inductive hypothesis gives the shape at the later steps, the\nshape-level corner condition transfers to the tableau through `isCorner_iff_shape`, brick 14's\n`uninsertSteps_invariants` then supplies `ColStrict` and `NoEmptyRows` at that intermediate tableau,\nand brick 17's `tableauShape_uninsert` advances the shape by one `removeCorner`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.shapeCornersAlong_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.shapeCornersAlong_cons","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedShapeRun.lean#L69-L72","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.shapeCornersAlong_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.shapeCornersAlong_nil","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedShapeRun.lean#L67-L67","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.ShapeCornersAlong","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.ShapeCornersAlong","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedShapeRun.lean#L61-L65","doc":"**The run-level corner condition, stated on shapes.** Every step names a corner of the shape as\nit stands at that step. Mirrors `CornersAlong` exactly, with the tableau replaced by its shape. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.removeCornerSteps_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.removeCornerSteps_cons","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedShapeRun.lean#L58-L59","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.removeCornerSteps_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.removeCornerSteps_nil","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedShapeRun.lean#L56-L56","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.removeCornerSteps","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.removeCornerSteps","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedShapeRun.lean#L50-L54","doc":"Peel the corners named by `is` off a shape, later steps first — the shape-level mirror of\n`uninsertSteps`' tableau component. ","signatureChunk":0}]}